      "title": "Pixelated 121: Is Googlebook the first real post-smartphone PC?",
      "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2024/03/Pixelated-cover.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Welcome to Pixelated episode 121. This week, Abner, Damien, and Will dive deep into Google’s new laptop platform, Googlebook. From hardware impressions across review units to making sense of the earliest days of desktop Android, there’s a ton of ground to cover. What sort of future awaits Googlebook, and is it right for what you want out of a laptop? You’ll need to listen to find out.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Enjoy the show? You can listen to our weekly members-only Pixelated Pro bonus episode by <a href=\"https://9to5google.com/pro/\">signing up for 9to5Google Pro</a> for just $5 per month, or about $1 per episode.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Sponsored by Proton Unlimited</strong>: Pixelated listeners can save 30% on an annual subscription to the company’s suite of privacy-friendly services by <a href=\"https://proton.me/9to5google\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">signing up using our link</a>. Thanks to Proton Unlimited for sponsoring the podcast.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-audio\"><audio controls src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/10/pix.mp3\"></audio></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-subscribe\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Subscribe</h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLcKP282Ii48tKK_KUt1kq1Ist9FkYR6lO\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">YouTube Podcasts</a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://pca.st/podcast/ac8e6ce0-06b1-0136-c264-7d73a919276a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Pocket Casts</a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/show/7pMiADiw0KAEW9Tg9UAEnZ?si=y8-L9zobTTucmjDVvMJOoQ&amp;dl_branch=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Spotify</a></li>\n\n\n\n<li>Am